  "answer_text": "The verifier rejects calling `helper_a()` inside an IRQ-disabled region because `helper_a` is a sleepable global function (it calls `bpf_copy_from_user`, which can sleep), and sleeping is not allowed with IRQs disabled.\n\nThe fix is to move the `helper_a(0)` call outside the IRQ-disabled critical section:\n\n```c\nSEC(\"?syscall\")\nint entry(void *ctx)\n{\n\tunsigned long flags;\n\n\thelper_a(0);\n\tbpf_local_irq_save(&flags);\n\tbpf_local_irq_restore(&flags);\n\treturn 0;\n}\n```",
